For the pension system, this creates a funding need that can be resolved if:

- the contribution rate increases from 30% in 2025 to 39% in 2085, while maintaining a replacement rate of 60% and a retirement age of 63;
- or if the replacement rate is reduced from 60% in 2025 to 46.2% in 2085, while keeping the contribution rate at 30% and the retirement age at 63;
- or if the retirement age rises from 63 in 2025 to 66.3 in 2085, while keeping the contribution rate at 30% and the replacement rate at 60%.
